{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T09:51:28.097Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-vcs-rd82"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Keep test children from delivering pm telemetry and Sentry reports"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"test/served-defects.test.ts labelled its installed-CLI children PM_TELEMETRY_SOURCE_CONTEXT=test (plus PM_TELEMETRY_INLINE_FLUSH=1) to avoid the detached flusher. Under pm-cli's documented policy a valid explicit source-context label permits intentional test delivery even under NODE_ENV=test, so the suite's expected vcs fetch/push/clone/remote refusals reached the production Sentry project as ExtensionCommandError (environment=test). CI runs on 2026-11-04 00:26-03:45Z created PM-CLI-3R, 3S, 3T, 3V, 3W and 3X, which blocked pm-cli's Auto Release Sentry gate for 2026.11.4 (pm-cli#1659). GitHub: unbraind/pm-vcs#176."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","sentry","telemetry","testing"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-04T09:51:28.097Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T09:51:28.097Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-hub"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"testEnvironment() adds the hard opt-out PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1, which no source-context label or PM_TELEMETRY_SEND_TEST_EVENTS overrides; served-defects drops the label; a regression test routes the event endpoint and SENTRY_DSN to a local collector, proves the route before any delivery-capable command, and shows a labelled child reports telemetry disabled and sends zero requests, failing when the opt-out is removed."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"No test child process delivers telemetry events or Sentry reports to production collectors."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"test/helpers"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6c0816dcb546a8b66c853b7902961015aa9bd74709278c5ea739c24e3df2cb75","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ac2b6491c0edd5cea9613e9fea9f763ba9234b26ea5aa291a68ecc2f631b31d4"}
