{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T10:43:42.513Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T10:43:42.513Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:43:42.513Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Verified 2026-11-04 on pm-cli 2026.10.30. The regression passes with the fix. With PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED removed from testEnvironment it fails: a labelled child reports enabled=true, and its requests reach only the local collector. Experiment with the old served-defects env: one failing pm get produced 3 POST /v1/events to the local collector, and 0 with PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1. Trap: a project settings telemetry.endpoint is ignored; only the global profile under PM_GLOBAL_PATH is honored, so the test proves the route before any delivery-capable command (filed upstream as pm-cli#1660). All 18 test files that spawn the installed pm CLI pass: 420/420. served-defects passes for node and bun. test-environment.test.ts 6/6. typecheck, lint, docstring and duplicates pass."}]}],"before_hash":"3942c210efdc83802e56e8edc3e89437f7c6051d170a613afd09ef1976057409","after_hash":"897eab4e9644af061c5d7e9c757a8344edcdfb498ddc8b830b5d5df9fcc68a38","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ed3de56e2e8352873c1199d865af9f3394b505ebc5635e9c986d118fb1a37bdc"}
